diff --git a/shell/plugins/bar/README.md b/shell/plugins/bar/README.md
index 41eb5f7a3..a7d0d28f1 100644
--- a/shell/plugins/bar/README.md
+++ b/shell/plugins/bar/README.md
@@ -12,6 +12,16 @@ the shell for its whole session.
 - The bar receives its config from the host shell as a `barConfig` property; the host loads it from `~/.config/omarchy/shell.json` (or `config/omarchy/shell.json` when the user has no file).
 - `omarchy bar position` updates only the user shell.json file.
 
+## Floating bar (niri port)
+
+This port floats the strip off the screen edge instead of drawing it flush:
+
+- `bar.floatGap` (defaults to the compositor's outer gap, currently 8) and `bar.cornerRadius` in `shell.json`; `noRoundedOnNoGaps` squares the strip when the gap is zero.
+- The layer surface is sized `thickness + floatGap`. Sizing it to `thickness` alone clips the strip's bottom edge and leaves an empty band under it; `exclusiveZone` uses the same combined size.
+- There is no compositor shadow on `^omarchy-bar$`. The strip's own 1px top highlight and bottom shade carry the edge; a 30px soft shadow read as an extra background band around the floating strip.
+- Bar-widget popups (`KeyboardPanel`) and the notification deck add `bar.floatGap` to their bar-edge offset, so they clear the floating strip instead of overlapping it by the gap.
+- The bar has no client frost region: niri's `ext_background_effect` mask cannot antialias the rounded end caps, and the stepped edge showed through the translucent fill. The fill gradient and 1px edge profile carry the bar. Widget popups still hand over an explicit `x/y/width/height` rect plus `radius`; Quickshell ignores `Region.radius` when the region is bound with `item`.
+
 ## Customizing
 
 The bar config lives under the `bar:` key of [`~/.config/omarchy/shell.json`](../../../docs/omarchy-shell.md#shelljson). Out of the box the shell uses [`config/omarchy/shell.json`](../../../config/omarchy/shell.json). Once you customize anything via the bar gestures, `omarchy bar ...`, or by editing shell.json directly, your file is canonical — there is no deep-merge.
